From 99d3e3d4136fe55909d065aca604819c51fa5842 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shaul Lavochkin <shaul9191@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 08:58:49 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 14/14] wasm: record await spans for run-time AsyncLocalStorage hooks

A scoped parser collector records each `await` expression's keyword start
and operand end, each `for await` loop's start (its outermost label) and
body span, and the argument span of each call to the bare identifier
`eval`, using the end of the previous token the lexer now keeps. 0010's
collector shares its restore guard. With BUNWASM_AWAIT_HOOKS on, the
printer passes a direct eval's argument through `__bunwasm_evalSource`,
so the browser engine can splice its AsyncLocalStorage hooks into source
compiled at run time while the call stays a direct eval.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
